{
  "id": "wasi-host-from-layer",
  "goals": [
    "(env : Wasm.HostEnv (Observed World)).Satisfies m (Verified.Wasi.hostSpecWith host calls) for an environment built on a lower layer",
    "a WASI host whose relations state the events of a lower layer that each WASI event makes",
    "Exec (linuxHost F L I replies) action w trace outcome w' → the world's events grow by images of trace",
    "NativeFunctionResult host startSignature ... → a statement about the host's world at the run's end",
    "LeanExe.Linux.Memory over Wasm.Mem",
    "LeanExe.Linux.readData fd events = the bytes that the WASI trace's events read from fd",
    "a host relation that would need a property of the store, such as a memory within a cap",
    "a host whose world is a log of lower events and has no exit marker",
    "sysContract (linuxHost F L I replies) call before args (invoke before args) for a flat call",
    "Host.sys_reports for a host whose reported sizes come partly from a parameter",
    "a host whose image of a call depends on the lower events before it",
    "a loop of lower calls inside one WASI call, such as getrandom until the buffer is full",
    "a lower event that records the bytes of its output region before the call",
    "a trace of images names only the descriptors that the host holds open"
  ],
